      <p class="article-intro">wa.me is the official WhatsApp short domain for click-to-chat links. Here is everything you need to know about the format, how to create one, and how to use it for your business.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What does wa.me mean?</h2>
      <p>wa.me is a short URL domain owned and operated by WhatsApp (Meta). It stands for "WhatsApp me" — a click-to-chat link that opens a WhatsApp conversation directly to a phone number when tapped.</p>
      <p>When you visit or share a wa.me link, WhatsApp opens on the device and starts a new chat with the specified number — without the person needing to save the contact first.</p>

      <h2>The wa.me link format</h2>
      <pre><code>https://wa.me/[full phone number with country code]</code></pre>
      <p>Examples:</p>
      <pre><code>India (+91):    https://wa.me/919876543210
USA (+1):       https://wa.me/19876543210
UAE (+971):     https://wa.me/971501234567
UK (+44):       https://wa.me/447911123456</code></pre>

      <h2>wa.me with a pre-filled message</h2>
      <p>Add <code>?text=</code> followed by your URL-encoded message:</p>
      <pre><code>https://wa.me/919876543210?text=Hi%20I%20want%20to%20enquire</code></pre>
      <p>Use <a href="/">LinkWA</a> to generate this automatically — just type your message normally and the tool handles URL encoding.</p>

      <h2>wa.me vs api.whatsapp.com — what is the difference?</h2>
      <p>WhatsApp provides two official link formats:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>https://wa.me/number</code> — the short form, recommended for most uses</li>
        <li><code>https://api.whatsapp.com/send?phone=number</code> — the older long form, still works but not preferred</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Both work identically. The wa.me format is shorter, cleaner, and better for printing and sharing.</p>

      <h2>Does wa.me work on desktop?</h2>
      <p>Yes. On desktop, clicking a wa.me link opens WhatsApp Web or the WhatsApp desktop app if installed. If WhatsApp is not set up on that device, the user is prompted to scan a QR code with their phone.</p>

      <h2>wa.me for WhatsApp Business</h2>
      <p>WhatsApp Business accounts use the same wa.me link format as personal accounts. Simply use your WhatsApp Business phone number. The link will open WhatsApp Business on devices where it is installed, and regular WhatsApp on others.</p>

      <h2>Can I create a wa.me link for a group?</h2>
      <p>No. wa.me links only work for individual phone numbers. WhatsApp group invite links use a different format: <code>https://chat.whatsapp.com/[invite code]</code>.</p>

      <h2>Is wa.me safe?</h2>
      <p>Yes. wa.me is an official WhatsApp domain operated by Meta. It does not collect any data beyond what WhatsApp normally collects when you open a chat. The link itself does not grant any access to your account or data.</p>

      <h2>How to create a wa.me link for free</h2>
